=== Text #1 ===
> APSA empowers urban slum communities towards social transformation through education, awareness,[ skill] training[ &] livelihoods.
APSA works with urban poor slums in 4 thematic areas – child rights, gender rights, youth empowerment and alcohol and substance abuse prevention – with priority for the[ girl] child,[ through] 20+[ institutional and community] outreachprojects,[ including] the non-form[al] Dream School, Nammane Open Shelter for children[ needing] care and protection, Navajeevana Nilayaworking hostel for young women trainees[ into] their[ first] jobs, Kaush[aly]a that[ provides skill] training to disadvantaged youth and the 24x7 Childline for children in distress. APSA is one of[ few NGOs] in the[ state] to work on child trafficking and the KishoriKanasu project[ at the] Suraksha Open Shelter in Kanakpura[ provides] protection and support for adolescent girl survivors of trafficking.
